        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MIROC-ESM",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "low amplitude of ENSO variation",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The largest climatic variability in the atmosphere-ocean system is ENSO. The amplitudes of the ENSO variation for the 0 ka simulations using MIROC-ESM and MIROC3 are smaller than what was observed (standard deviation of 0.39 and 0.48, respectively, as opposed to 0.92 for ECMWF 40 yr Re-analyses; Roxy et al., 2011).",
